{"_id":"68a7363c8ec3d8323af1f12b","nodeId":"HhICJpCK5__b-itUoEBES","roadmapSlug":"sql","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:40.099Z","description":"# HAVING\n\nThe `HAVING` clause in SQL is used to filter the results of aggregate functions. It's similar to the `WHERE` clause, but operates on grouped rows produced by the `GROUP BY` clause. Essentially, `HAVING` allows you to specify conditions that groups must meet to be included in the final result set after aggregation has taken place.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"SQL HAVING Clause","url":"https://www.programiz.com/sql/having","_id":"69bba6b933a0ad7a57afe6d5"},{"type":"video","title":"HAVING Clause","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tYBOMw7Ob8E","_id":"69bba6b933a0ad7a57afe6d6"}],"updatedAt":"2026-03-19T07:33:13.507Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04dcfb5fcb94d0416838","title":"DataCamp - SQL Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/ZVeXng"},{"_id":"6a5e04dcfb5fcb94d04167c7","title":"roadmap.sh - Master SQL","partner":"roadmap.sh","type":"course","url":"https://roadmap.sh/courses/sql"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/sql/content/HhICJpCK5__b-itUoEBES.md"}